  "title": "Observability Fundamentals",
  "description": "Learn the three pillars of observability: logs, metrics, traces.",
  "order": 1,
  "difficulty": "intermediate",
  "estimatedMinutes": 16,
  "tags": ["observability", "pillars", "fundamentals"],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Observability is the ability to understand system state from its outputs. The three pillars are logs, metrics, and traces."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Key Concepts"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "key-terms",
      "data": {
        "terms": [
          {
            "term": "Observability",
            "definition": "The ability to infer system state from outputs."
          },
          {
            "term": "Logs",
            "definition": "Discrete events with timestamps."
          },
          {
            "term": "Metrics",
            "definition": "Numeric values aggregated over time."
          },
          {
            "term": "Traces",
            "definition": "End-to-end request paths through services."
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Three Pillars"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "data": {
        "headers": ["Pillar", "Description", "Best For"],
        "rows": [
          ["Logs", "Discrete events", "Debugging, audit"],
          ["Metrics", "Aggregated numbers", "Alerting, trends"],
          ["Traces", "Request paths", "Latency analysis"]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Logs"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Logs are timestamped records of events. They are best for debugging and auditing, but hard to aggregate across services."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Metrics"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Metrics are numeric values aggregated over time (counts, rates, percentiles). They are best for alerting and identifying trends."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Traces"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Traces follow a request through multiple services. They show the path and latency at each step, making them ideal for latency analysis."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "RED Method"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "The RED method defines three key metrics per service: Rate (requests per second), Errors (error rate), Duration (latency percentiles)."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Architecture"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "mermaid",
